  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that 7-Angeloylechinatine may interact with CD276 antigen through a series of molecular targets. The drug is shown to have targets in HaCaT cells and VMRC-LCP, both of which are implicated in the targeting of CD276 antigen. This implies that 7-Angeloylechinatine may act as a modulator of pathways involving CD276 antigen, potentially through indirect mechanisms. The evidence is consistent across different targets, suggesting a possible role in regulating CD276 antigen expression or function. The integration of these targets highlights a potential mechanism where 7-Angeloylechinatine influences cellular processes that ultimately affect CD276 antigen activity. The relationship is supported by the shared involvement of CD276 antigen in multiple pathways, reinforcing the likelihood of a functional link between the drug and the antigen.",
